  "description": "Cooking in summer is really hard labor. Whether you’re going to buy ingredients, doing something in front of a fire, or even dipping your hands in cold water and washing dishes, you’re sweating. It’s hard to eat and even have a fever in your body.\nHowever, the chef at the restaurant who arrived in the heat of the day said, “You can’t starve,” and she was introduced by a friend. Why do you feel like you’re in a relationship now? Can I start a new relationship?\n\n(Source: BOMTOON, translated)",
